/-! ## §1 — CROSS-TIE 1: the L4 universal exponent IS the reciprocal of ‖φ‖² (ASCENT ⊗ L4). -/

/-- ★★ CROSS-TIE 1 (never banked as a TYPE). The condensed-matter universal critical exponent
    (L4, N405) IS the RECIPROCAL of the banked octonion calibration-3-form norm `‖φ‖²`
    (N313, the ASCENT-side terminal invariant): `criticalExponent = 1 / assoc3NormSq = 1/42`;
    and that norm EQUALS the interaction-channel count `imChannelCount (finrank ℚ ImO)` (N314,
    the GATHER-side count). The universality number of the many-body scale is the terminal
    algebra's own structure-form norm — one `42`, read as a 3-form norm and as an off-diagonal
    pair count. -/
theorem exponent_is_structure_form_norm_reciprocal :
    criticalExponent = 1 / assoc3NormSq
      ∧ assoc3NormSq = 42
      ∧ assoc3NormSq = (imChannelCount (Module.finrank ℚ ImO) : ℚ) := by
  refine ⟨?_, assoc3NormSq_eq_42, ?_⟩
  · rw [criticalExponent_eq_one_div_42, assoc3NormSq_eq_42]
  · rw [channels_O_eq_assoc3NormSq]

/-! ## §2 — CROSS-TIE 2: the ONE terminal dimension 7 threads L2, L3, L4. -/

/-- ★★ CROSS-TIE 2 (never banked as a TYPE). The SINGLE terminal imaginary dimension
    `finrank ℚ ImO = 7` threads three arc-L rungs simultaneously:
      · L2 (shell closure) — the antisymmetric exterior power VANISHES beyond capacity:
        `⋀^N ImO = 0` for every `N > 7`;
      · L3 (chemical periodicity) — the modular occupancy RECURS with period `7`:
        `⋀^((Z+7) % 7) ImO` has the same dimension as `⋀^(Z % 7) ImO`;
      · L4 (universality) — the interaction-channel count is the ordered off-diagonal pair count
        `7·6 = 42`.
    Three emergent structures (atomic capacity, chemical recurrence, critical universality) are
    read off ONE dimension of the terminal carrier. -/
theorem terminal_dim_threads_ladder :
    Module.finrank ℚ ImO = 7
    ∧ (∀ {N : ℕ}, 7 < N → finrank ℚ (⋀[ℚ]^N Phys.Algebra.ImO) = 0)
    ∧ (∀ Z : ℕ, finrank ℚ (⋀[ℚ]^((Z + 7) % 7) Phys.Algebra.ImO)
          = finrank ℚ (⋀[ℚ]^(Z % 7) Phys.Algebra.ImO))
    ∧ imChannelCount (Module.finrank ℚ ImO)
        = Module.finrank ℚ ImO * (Module.finrank ℚ ImO - 1)
    ∧ imChannelCount (Module.finrank ℚ ImO) = 42 :=
  ⟨finrank_ImO, fun h => imO_closes_beyond_seven h,
   imO_valenceSector_dim_periodic, imChannelCount_eq_n_times_n_sub_one _, channels_O⟩

/-! ## §3 — CROSS-TIE 3: the ONE cause (non-associativity) drives L1 and L4. -/

/-- ★★ CROSS-TIE 3 (never banked as a TYPE). The terminal-algebra LOSS of associativity — the
    genuinely new cascade termination `not_associative` on `O ℚ` — is the ONE cause behind two
    utterly different arc-L rungs:
      · L1 (nuclear residual colour) — the composite obstruction associator is genuinely NONZERO
        at the cascade-stop witness `(ιJ, e₂, e₂)` (the residual nuclear force is real);
      · L4 (universality) — via its structure-3-form norm `‖φ‖² = assoc3NormSq`, the SAME
        non-associativity fixes the universal critical exponent `criticalExponent = 1/‖φ‖²`.
    One termination, two emergent rungs. -/
theorem ladder_one_cause_nonassociativity :
    (assoc (1 + (CD.iota (ιJ ℚ) : O ℚ)) (1 + (CD.iota (CD.e2 : H ℚ) : O ℚ))
        (CD.e2 : O ℚ) ≠ 0)
    ∧ (¬ ∀ x y z : O ℚ, (x * y) * z = x * (y * z))
    ∧ criticalExponent = 1 / assoc3NormSq := by
  refine ⟨Phys.Algebra.NuclearResidual.composite_residual_nonvanishing,
          not_associative, ?_⟩
  rw [criticalExponent_eq_one_div_42, assoc3NormSq_eq_42]

/-! ## §4 — THE CAPSTONE (non-hollow) + W8 non-vacuity. -/

/-- ★★★ THE EMERGENT MATTER LADDER, CONSOLIDATED (arc-L L5 capstone). The four rungs are ONE
    fold engine — the terminated Cayley-Dickson cascade — read at four many-body scales. Bundled
    over the derived ℝ `Cut` and the banked concrete octonion objects:
